                                "sense_id": "df16cf21-da4d-3a2d-b4aa-93797fa7bd99",
                                "text": "Weevil larvae are apodous; in contrast, most scarab larvae bear six hooklike legs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94be6632-6218-4050-ae30-6b9b029b94f4",
                                "sense_id": "df16cf21-da4d-3a2d-b4aa-93797fa7bd99",
                                "text": "Snakes, worms, certain fish, and other limbless creatures are all apodous, while visibly similar creatures (such as millipedes or centipedes) use a different type of movement called a metachronal gait."
                            }
                        ]
